  "ruledOut": [
    "Native tangent stream is valid: four(1,0,0,-1), normals(0,0,-1), no basis repair occurred. The zero-TBN hypothesis is contradicted by actual input receipts and is withdrawn.",
    "Real light is Directional white2, Hard shadow, rotation50/-30, normalbias0, cullingMask4(layer2). FxLightMode1 and legacy onlyBlinn keywordtrue. Unlit-only setup is not the current cause.",
    "Fixture source control is SetFloat_BumpScale0 -> Capture -> Draw -> restore1 after capture. For normalcase GeometryFrameState null; Capture only writes displayFrame and invokes Camera.Render. No fixture callback resetsScale1 in between.",
    "Actor output is present: independent actor-only visibility660/1015 and exact parity/repeat. Full frame includes actor, so this is not merely comparing a receiver-only shadow.",
    "Generated Forward call has226 arguments matching product signature; BumpMapToggle index148 comes from_BumpMapToggle, BumpTex149 from_BumpTex, BumpScale150 from_BumpScale, normals/tangents from IN and FxLightMode154 from_FxLightMode. No static miswiring found.",
    "Legacy/Frozen properties and fragment use same_BumpTex/_BumpScale names; _NORMALMAP samples then DecodeNormalMapV2 updates normalWS before lighting/Fresnel. Shared normal decode uses scale in supportedPacking code. No reviewed feature source overwrite of BumpScale in this path."
  ],
  "unprovenBoundary": {
    "point": "Actual render-time texture/normal enable and control uniform uptake -> sampled/decode normals -> visible normal consumers",
    "missingEvidence": [
      "Actual_NORMALMAP keyword and_BumpMapToggle immediately at each on/off draw (not only the setup statement)",
      "GetTexture_BumpTex object identity/name/texel content atdraw",
      "GetFloat_BumpScale afterSet0 and directly before/off-draw",
      "GPU sampled normal/decoded NormalTS/NormalWS or actual material constant-buffer state"
    ],
    "reason": "Existing receipts capture_BumpScale=1 before control, light metadata and CPU mesh stream. They do not capture control-time0 or actual sampled normals. Static setters/generated wires are not GPU uptake proof. Persistent three-way0 response alone cannot distinguish binding/cache/baseline behavior from a consumer issue."
  },
  "status": "No claimed Graph functional gap, no new supported-normal conclusion. Keep both old and latest Failed XML and strict strong response assertion. Do not lowerthreshold, disable finite/visible or retry weak controls blindly. Continue unrelated implementation and bounded DN0 product integration; G4 full lighting support remains incomplete.",
